      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is about 5 times the usual maximum metformin dose. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 4250 mg dose is also far above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is serious, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possibilities are:\n- **850 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **425 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals, which isn't a standard tablet strength but could be given as a split dose\n- **500 mg** by mouth two or three times daily with meals\n\nPlease tell me the dose you intended. If 4250 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I would still want to flag it for pharmacy review before entering it."
      }
     ],
